[498.316789, "o", "MARKET CLEARING ANALYSIS SUMMARY\r\n================================\r\n\r\nOBJECTIVE:\r\nAnalyze the impact of increasing the thermal capacity of transmission line 64-1501\r\nby 20% on the day-ahead market clearing results.\r\n\r\nMETHODOLOGY:\r\n- DC-OPF with reserve co-optimization\r\n- 2,869 buses, 510 generators, 4,582 transmission lines\r\n- Reserve requirement: 5,923.5 MW\r\n- Thermal capacity limits enforced on all transmission lines\r\n- Spinning reserve with standard capacity coupling constraints\r\n\r\nKEY FINDINGS:\r\n\r\n1. BASE CASE (Original network):\r\n   - Total system cost: $2,546,267.27 per hour\r\n   - Binding transmission lines: 29 (at or near thermal limits)\r\n   - Line 64-1501 capacity: 312.00 MW\r\n   - Reserve clearing price: $5.00/MWh\r\n\r\n2. COUNTERFACTUAL CASE (Line 64-1501 capacity +20%):\r\n   - Total system cost: $2,546,126.85 per hour\r\n   - Binding transmission lines: 28 (one less than base case)\r\n   - Line 64-1501 capacity: 374.40 MW (20% increase)\r\n   - Reserve clearing price: $5.00/MWh\r\n\r\n3. IMPACT ANALYSIS:\r\n   - Cost reduction: $140.42 per hour\r\n   - Annual savings (estimated): $1,229,484.80\r\n   - Congestion relief: YES (binding lines reduced from 29 to 28)\r\n   - Line 64-1501 status: No longer binding in counterfactual\r\n\r\n4. LOCATIONAL MARGINAL PRICES (LMPs):\r\n   - Most buses show stable LMPs between scenarios\r\n   - Top 3 buses with largest LMP drops identified\r\n   - System-wide price changes reflect reduced congestion\r\n\r\nCONCLUSION:\r\nRelaxing the thermal capacity constraint on line 64-1501 by 20% reduces the\r\ntotal system cost by $140.42/hour and relieves one binding transmission constraint.\r\nThis suggests that line 64-1501 was indeed a significant source of congestion in\r\nthe base case, contributing to higher market clearing prices.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENATIONS:\r\n- Consider infrastructure investment to increase line 64-1501 capacity\r\n- Monitor line 64-1501 loading in real-time operations\r\n- Evaluate cost-benefit of capacity upgrade ($1.23M annual savings potential)\r\n\r\n"]
